<title>SINGAPORE: Easyknit offers 45 million new shares at HK$3.05.</title>
<headline>Easyknit offers 45 million new shares at HK$3.05.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Easyknit International Holdings Ltd said on Friday it was offering 45 million new shares at Hong Kong $3.05 each an initial public offer (IPO) for a secondary listing in Singapore.  </p>
<p>Easyknit, which is listed on the Stock Exchange of Hong Kong, said in a statement published in Singapore newspapers that 20 million shares would be offered to the public and 25 million shares via placement.</p>
<p>Easyknit sources and exports cotton-based knitted garments for women, children and infants, mostly to the United States.</p>
<p>OCBC Bank is lead underwriter for the issue.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom 65-8703080</p>
